From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eight <eight@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ASoC: amd: acp: add Huawei MateBook D14 AMD to config
 table

The Huawei MateBook D14 AMD laptop (DMI board/product name NBM-WXX9,
product version M1020) contains an ACP 3.x audio coprocessor (PCI ID
1022:15e2) with an ESS ES8336 codec attached via I2C. Without an entry
in snd_amd_acp_find_config()'s config_table[] the snd_acp_pci driver
rejects the device with -ENODEV, so the legacy snd_rn_pci_acp3x driver
claims it instead. That legacy path only registers the PDM (digital
microphone) frontend and no codec routing, leaving the machine without
speaker, headphone and internal microphone audio.

Add the board to the table with FLAG_AMD_LEGACY, matching its
ACP_PCI_DEV_ID device, so the acp3x-es83xx machine driver binds to the
ES8336 codec and exposes working playback and capture devices.

Signed-off-by: Eight <eight@localhost>
---
 sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c                        | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
--- a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
@@ -202,6 +202,20 @@
 			{}
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		.flags = FLAG_AMD_LEGACY,
+		.device = ACP_PCI_DEV_ID,
+		.dmi_table = (const struct dmi_system_id []) {
+			{
+				.matches = {
+					DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "HUAWEI"),
+					DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "NBM-WXX9"),
+					DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_VERSION, "M1020"),
+				},
+			},
+			{}
+		},
+	},
 };
 
 static int snd_amd_acp_acpi_find_config(struct pci_dev *pci)
